{
  "summary": "This experiment isolated the fusion mechanism by replacing concat with weighted fusion in the otherwise identical multimodal, multiprofile configuration (scvi_n200 + ResNet50, avgpool), directly comparable to llm_summary_007. Validation accuracy rose from ~63.2% to ~67.8% (F1 from ~60.7% to ~64.6%), a ~4.6-point gain attributable to the fusion change, and now exceeds the RNA-only multiprofile avgpool baseline (~65.0%, llm_summary_004) by ~2.8 points, indicating that the image modality does carry complementary signal that concat fails to exploit and that weighted fusion effectively down-weights the weaker image contribution. It remains uncertain whether attention-based or learned fusion could push further beyond ~67.8%, whether stronger image encoders or image-specific aggregation could amplify the residual image contribution, and whether this gain is stable across different data splits or task formulations."
}

